# Printable text and the C0 controls of M1.10, plus one soft wrap.
# VT100 User Guide, "Cursor Control": BS moves the cursor one column left,
# HT advances to the next tab stop (every eight columns by default), CR
# returns to column 1, LF moves down one line without changing the column.
# DEC STD 070: a character printed in the last column arms a deferred wrap;
# the next printable character starts a new row and the old row is soft
# wrapped.
hello\tworld\r\n
abcXY\b\b\bdef\r\n
wrap-around-x
